From 180c75c3227d222887e1d3eef1f5ecbf798dac56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Wiklander <jens.wiklander@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 18:40:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 904/913] core: fs_htree: prevent possible hash-tree reset

In tee_fs_htree_open() when checking if hash-tree head has only been
partially written, add that it can only be true without a provided hash.
A hash-tree head is always fully written if there's a hash over it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git a298c37f0a40f2e2df70bebd55911f9b7a5f1ebd core: fs_htree: prevent possible hash-tree reset]
Fixes: 5a9d570a8d7f ("core: fs_htree: re-init hash tree when both tag and counter are zero")
Change-Id: I87e0c6274779101010f026dfef9e788f324eb349
Signed-off-by: Jens Wiklander <jens.wiklander@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Jerome Forissier <jerome.forissier@arm.com>
(cherry picked from commit b4846822231bc08737f6e0e3f89c83e3aa14a53a)
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/613407
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Tested-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
---
 core/tee/fs_htree.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/tee/fs_htree.c b/core/tee/fs_htree.c
index ee86c6105..5215a2686 100644
--- a/core/tee/fs_htree.c
+++ b/core/tee/fs_htree.c
@@ -697,10 +697,15 @@ TEE_Result tee_fs_htree_open(bool create, uint8_t *hash, uint32_t min_counter,
 		/*
 		 * If a power loss occurred during hash tree creation, the
 		 * head may not have been written and counter is still 0.
-		 * Re-initialze the hash tree.
+		 * Re-initialize the hash tree.
+		 *
+		 * If hash is non-NULL, the head must have been written
+		 * properly at least once before. This prevents reset of
+		 * the hash tree only by overwriting selected parts of the
+		 * head.
 		 */
-		if (ht_head_is_partially_done(&ht->head)) {
-			res = create_and_sync(&ht, hash, min_counter);
+		if (!hash && ht_head_is_partially_done(&ht->head)) {
+			res = create_and_sync(&ht, NULL, min_counter);
 			if (res != TEE_SUCCESS)
 				goto out;
 		}
